Z||000078||Jay||07-02-2001||08:26 PM||||That just shows your ignorance on the subject of race.  Malcolm X may have started out with racist views (can you blame him for hating whites?)but by the end of his life he was a mainstream practicing muslim with NO racist views.  Read the autobiography of his life as dictated to Alex Haley and you will understand the transformation he made.  The problem with this world is that people never allow others to grow and change, they are always remembered for the bad in their lives.  Malcolm X was not a racist but a believer in the black community.  Was he a racist at one time?  YES, he even admitted it himself.  Was all that he spewed out racist?  NO.  I wouldn't think that many non ethnic people would understand, but at least have a base line understanding before making a broad statement like the one above.  Malcolm X is the perfect example of what can happen when people listen to each other with open minds and have a sincere desire to understand.  Calling him a racist idiot is being one yourself.||||reg||1
